  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nThe main theme for the long term forecast is warm and dry conditions \nexpected to continue through the weekend with the possible return of \nprecipitation early next week. The upper ridging mentioned in the \nshort term discussion will persist across the region over the \nweekend. This will keep highs in the 80s to lower 90s and near zero \nprecipitation chances everyday through the weekend. By early next \nweek, an upper pattern change could bring shower and thunderstorm \nchances. Over the weekend, an upper trough will dig down the western \ncoast before stalling off the coast of SoCal. This will shift flow \naloft to the southwest ushering subtropical moisture. Models also \nindicate a hurricane may track north along Mexico which could in \nturn aid with increasing moisture to the mid-to-upper levels. The \ninflux of moisture and multiple passing shortwaves could bring \nwidespread precipitation chances daily beginning Tuesday. However, \ndo not get your hopes up just yet. This is still a little less than \na week out and can expect changes to the forecast as we get closer. \nAlong with precipitation chances, we could also see cooler \ntemperatures with highs in the 70s to 80s.",
